A `<?start name=…> … <?end>` MarkerRegion lays out like a fragment: the open PI,
an indented child list, and the `<?end>` close aligned back at the open's
column. A block-level child (here another region) forces the break regardless
of width, and nesting reindents each level independently — same machinery as
Element/Fragment, just with a PI open/close instead of `<tag>`/`<>`.

-- input.gsx --
package ui

component Page(id string) {
<?start name="panel">
			<p>loading</p>
<?start name={id}>
						<span>nested</span>
	<?end>
			<?end>
}
-- fmt.golden --
package ui

component Page(id string) {
	<?start name="panel">
		<p>loading</p>
		<?start name={id}>
			<span>nested</span>
		<?end>
	<?end>
}
